  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In a wave equation, <math><mi>x</mi></math> and <math><mi>t</mi></math> must be related in the form <math><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. Therefore, we rewrite the given equation as<br /><br /><math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />For <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> it becomes <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />And for <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, it becomes<br /><br /><math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> or <math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>",
